A parent component updates its own state. Its child takes no props and is not wrapped in `React.memo`. What happens to the child?

```jsx
function Child() {
  console.log('Child rendered');
  return <p>Static text</p>;
}

function Parent() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
  return (
    <>
      <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>{count}</button>
      <Child />
    </>
  );
}
```

`Box` is wrapped in `React.memo`. Its parent re-renders because of unrelated state. Does `Box` re-render?

```jsx
const Box = memo(function Box({ style }) {
  return <div style={style} />;
});

function Parent() {
  const [n, setN] = useState(0);
  return (
    <>
      <button onClick={() => setN(n + 1)}>{n}</button>
      <Box style={{ color: 'red' }} />
    </>
  );
}
```

`Card` is memoized, and the parent passes it some JSX as children. The parent re-renders with unrelated state. Does `Card` skip the render?

